{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Warcraft Reborn characters switch between up to 20 specializations, each with its own build, action bars and equipment set link",
  "contract": [
    "The client's specialization list (SpecializationUtil) offers #SPEC_SWAP_SPELLS = 20 specializations; spec 1 is always unlocked and spec N needs swap spell N. Activating one casts that swap spell (CastSpecialSpell); the active spec is only learned from SMSG 0x725, which also fires ASCENSION_CA_SPECIALIZATION_ACTIVE_ID_CHANGED (equip the spec's set, activate its Mystic Enchant preset).",
    "A Warcraft Reborn character keeps its talents as a free-pick build, so it switches specializations like a free-pick Hero: each slot keeps its own build and action bars; trainer spells are shared; the stock talent spec is not used.",
    "Before the fix the swap spells fell through to the stock dual-spec switch: Specialization II changed the stock talent group, III to XX did nothing, and 0x725 was never sent.",
    "The per-specialization equipment set link (CMSG 0x73A { u32 spec-1, u8 linked, [u64 set guid] }) is saved and echoed as SMSG 0x738 with the same layout, and resent at world entry; a set the character does not own is refused.",
    "The swap spells have a 5 s cast time (SpellCastTimes 6), like the stock 63644; every check after a cast waits for it.",
    "Deleting a linked set leaves the link pointing at nothing: a set marked deleted (until the next save) cannot be linked, and a link whose set no longer exists is cleared at world entry instead of being resent."
  ],
  "timeout_ms": 180000,
  "players": [
    {
      "id": "w",
      "name": "Rebornslots",
      "race": 1,
      "class": 1,
      "level": 60,
      "security": 2
    }
  ],
  "steps": [
